      "writtenOn": "2022-01-27T23:28:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "brya has both setups, so it\u0027s no longer a nice-to-have.\nhowever, for a given port, only one of the two schemes applies,\nso, we need the port flag to tell us how to handle it.\n\nthe open question here is whether there could be a valid configuration\nwhere a single port would require\nCONFIG_USB_PD_FRS_PPC and CONFIG_USB_PD_FRS_TCPC.\ni suspect that such a config won\u0027t make sense.\n\nguybrush is the only board that turns on CONFIG_USB_PD_FRS_TCPC\nand it does not use CONFIG_USB_PD_FRS_PPC.",
      "parentUuid": "7c573d07_18cc3afc",
